    "title": "Nancy Millis",
    "text": "Nancy Millis, 94, passed away peacefully Saturday, Nov. 15, 2025, at her home in Westerly, R.I.\nBorn in North Adams, Mass., Nancy was the daughter of Agnes (LaBleau) and Daniel Millis.\nShe lived most of her adult life in Great Barrington, Mass. until she moved with her sister, Helen, to Jamestown, R.I. in 1995 to be close to their family.\nThe youngest of 10 children, Nancy was predeceased by sisters Helen DeTour, Dorothy McSheen, Anna Sweeney, Mary Trottier and brothers William, Francis, James, Robert and John Millis.\nShe was the beloved Aunt Nancy to Thomas DeTour and his wife, Christine, their sons Michael, Daniel and his wife KerriAnne, as well as great-grandnephew and niece, Joseph and Carolyn. She also leaves her nieces Carolyn Flemings, Elaine MacGregor and a large extended family, as well as dear friends, Rene Daponte and Linda Browning.\nNancy loved gardening, decorating for Christmas and family celebrations. With the support of Bridges and Looking Upwards staff, she made many lasting friendships and became confident in living independently in her Pemberton Avenue apartment.\nIn recent years, Nancy became a cherished member of the Fairfield Avenue Group Home in Westerly. She leaves her group home family, Jay, Theresa and Lisa, as well as caring and dedicated staff, Greg, Lisa, Clara, Kaleigh and Mark.\nThe DeTour family extends their heartfelt gratitude to the entire group home staff and Hope Health Hospice staff for their exceptional care of Nancy.\nVisitation will be from 2-4 p.m. Saturday, Nov. 22, 2025, in the Fagan-Quinn Funeral Home of Patrick Quinn Funerals and Cremations, 825 Boston Neck Road, North Kingstown, R.I.\nIn lieu of flowers, please consider a donation in memory of Nancy to Looking Upwards, P.O. Box 4289, Middletown, RI 02842.\nKindly visit the Fagan-Quinn Funeral Home for complete obituary and online condolences, www.PatrickQuinnFuneralsandCremations.com.",
